    "title": "E-scooter death on Farmers - NewsBreak",
    "text": "1 days ago A 60-year-old St. Albans man has died after allegedly getting rammed earlier in the month by a Ram ProMaster 1500 cargo van while driving a stand-up e-scooter. Tyler Pope, of 191st Street, died Sept. 16 in Jamaica Hospital Medical Center after getting hit Aug. 28 while traveling southbound on Farmers Boulevard. The van allegedly ran into Pope while the van driver was making a left turn on Merrick Boulevard, per 113th Precinct cops. Read full article",
